# Power BI local artifacts (never commit these)
# The whole .pbi/ tree is Desktop-generated runtime state: settings, caches and the
# per-user editor layout. None of it belongs in version control, and the layout files in
# particular churn on every open/save, so tracking them produces noisy diffs.
**/.pbi/
*.pbix

# Diagram / layout state - Desktop rewrites these on every save, so they only create diff noise
diagramLayout.json
semanticModelDiagramLayout.json

# IDE folders Desktop may create next to the PBIP
.vscode/
.idea/

# Agent validation output
.bpa/
bpa-results.json
*-audit-report.md
*-audit-report.json
duckdb-Feature-Addition-plan.md
duckdb-pending-linux-verification.md

# Rendered-output verification (scripts/capture_report_screenshot.py, Windows-only).
# Regenerate locally; PNGs are throwaway evidence, not source.
artifacts/

# Environment / secrets
.env
secrets/

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
*.swp
*.swo

# Local sample data (large binaries; regenerate or fetch separately)
data/*.xlsx
data/*.csv
data/*.parquet

# Local source assets for extending the visual gallery; check in PBIR examples, not packages.
#
# The folder itself is ignored, but four things inside it are contracts rather than
# payload, so they are negated back in below. Keeping them tracked is what lets a
# clone describe and verify the gallery without a single binary present:
#
#   manifest.csv        the fetch contract: URL, version, GUID, SHA-256 per asset
#   content.json        the authored prose the catalog is generated from
#   visual-catalog.json the derived description the gallery and allowlist both read
#   Images/             thumbnail art for the 26 custom visuals
#   icons/              vendored chart-type SVGs (MIT) for the native visuals
#   PBIR/               reference report definitions, staged by
#                       scripts/stage_pbir_examples.py from the third-party PBIPs
#
# Still ignored, deliberately: PBIVIZ/ and PBIX/ (publisher binaries and sample
# workbooks, fetched by scripts/fetch_gallery_assets.py).
#
# The pattern excludes the folder's *contents* rather than the folder itself. Git
# does not descend into an excluded directory, so `!file` rules underneath one are
# silently inert - re-inclusion only works if the parent directory stays visible.
samples/visual-gallery-assets/*
!samples/visual-gallery-assets/manifest.csv
!samples/visual-gallery-assets/content.json
!samples/visual-gallery-assets/visual-catalog.json
!samples/visual-gallery-assets/EXCEPTIONS.md
!samples/visual-gallery-assets/Images/
!samples/visual-gallery-assets/icons/
!samples/visual-gallery-assets/PBIR/
# Playwright CLI output (may contain credentials)
.playwright-cli/
# Personal local agent config (personal skills, tooling)
.claude/

# Custom visual packages (publisher binaries, e.g. Microsoft AppSource .pbiviz).
# VisualGallery reports reference custom visuals by GUID in
# report.json -> publicCustomVisuals; the packages themselves are downloaded by
# scripts/fetch_gallery_assets.py and installed by scripts/extract_custom_visuals.py.
# Never committed.
*.pbiviz
**/CustomVisuals/
